<title>USA: Carter-Wallace Q2 shr $0.12 vs loss $0.10.</title>
<headline>Carter-Wallace Q2 shr $0.12 vs loss $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carter-Wallace Inc</p>
<p>					   SUMMARY OF OPERATING RESULTS</p>
<p>						  THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>					 Sep 30, 1996	Sep 30, 1995</p>
<p> Sales				$ 159,532,000     $ 154,810,000</p>
<p> Earnings Before One-Time	   9,493,000	   8,831,000</p>
<p>Charges and Taxes</p>
<p> One-Time Charges			  --	(16,500,000) (a)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) Before Taxes     9,493,000	 (7,669,000)</p>
<p> Income Taxes (Benefit)	     3,892,000	 (3,145,000)</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss)		  5,601,000	( 4,524,000)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) Per Share		  .12		( .10)</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	46,391,000	  46,113,000</p>
<p>						  SIX MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>					 Sep 30, 1996	Sep 30, 1995</p>
<p> Sales				 $329,421,000	$331,847,000</p>
<p>Earnings Before One-Time</p>
<p> Charges and Taxes		   25,188,000	  30,391,000</p>
<p> One-Time Charges			  --	(36,600,000) (a)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) Before Taxes    25,188,000	 (6,209,000)</p>
<p> Income Taxes (Benefit)	    10,327,000	 (2,546,000)</p>
<p> Net Earnings (Loss)		 14,861,000	( 3,663,000)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) Per Share		  .32		( .08)</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	46,389,000	  46,132,000</p>
<p>(a) In the prior year, the Company incurred one-time charges related to the closure of its condom manufacturing plant in Trenton, New Jersey and the restructuring of operations and facilities.  These one-time costs resulted in a pre-tax charge of $16,500,000 ($9,740,000 after tax or $.21 per share) in the quarter and a pre-tax charge of $36,600,000 ($21,600,000 after tax or $.47 per share) for the six months ended September 30, 1995. Carter-Wallace, Inc. markets toiletries, proprietary drugs, pharmaceuticals, diagnostic specialties and pet products.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
